From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Altera BMC <openbmc@altera.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Jun 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] psu: add TSC1641 to sensorTypes

The ST TSC1641 is the 60V/16-bit power monitor on the MikroE Current 12
Click (MIKROE-6065) used in the Step 4 demo, and on the Phase-2 Altera
sensor board. The Linux hwmon "tsc1641" driver exposes load voltage
(in0), current (curr1), power (power1) and temperature (temp1), but
psusensor's sensorTypes map did not list it, so an entity-manager
"TSC1641" Exposes entry was ignored.

Add the type so dbus-sensors instantiates the device with driver name
"tsc1641" (createsHWMon = true) and publishes its power telemetry on
D-Bus / Redfish.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Altera BMC <openbmc@altera.com>
---
 src/psu/PSUSensorMain.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/psu/PSUSensorMain.cpp b/src/psu/PSUSensorMain.cpp
index 42af138..f8f2f11 100644
--- a/src/psu/PSUSensorMain.cpp
+++ b/src/psu/PSUSensorMain.cpp
@@ -144,6 +144,7 @@ static const I2CDeviceTypeMap sensorTypes = {
     {"TPS25990", I2CDeviceType{"tps25990", true}},
     {"TPS53679", I2CDeviceType{"tps53679", true}},
     {"TPS546D24", I2CDeviceType{"tps546d24", true}},
+    {"TSC1641", I2CDeviceType{"tsc1641", true}},
     {"XDP710", I2CDeviceType{"xdp710", true}},
     {"XDPE11280", I2CDeviceType{"xdpe11280", true}},
     {"XDPE12284", I2CDeviceType{"xdpe12284", true}},
